summary:
  The buffer writer starts without the guard that stops it when its host dies.

history:
  Measured on the bench 2026-09-23: the viewer killed while a FLAC preview
  played through the relay, and the writer's shell went to systemd --user
  with the whole chain still copying the station at ~128 KiB/s, for nobody,
  until its hour cap. The guard beside every writer is what ends that within
  a few seconds of the host going.

target:
  package/contents/ui/TimeshiftLogic.js

find:
          + (o.guardPath ? "bash " + q(o.guardPath) + " watch \"$$\" \"$PPID\" \"$pid\" >/dev/null 2>&1 & " : "")

replace:
          + ""

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_timeshiftlogic.qml::test_every_writer_starts_its_guard_and_names_its_owner
  and tests/qml/tst_timeshiftengine.qml::test_every_run_command_starts_the_writers_guard.
  Line-neutral.
